# Every version docs/project-context.md claims, bound to the manifest entry that owns it.
#
# That page exists to tell an agent what its training data gets wrong about THIS stack, so a version
# it states is the whole of its value — and a stale one is worse than none, because it is asserted
# with the same confidence as a true one. Measured over the page's own history: ten drifted claims
# against ZERO wrong version numbers, which is why the numbers are gated here and the normative
# prose was moved to the docs that own it rather than gated in place.
#
# Format:  <manifest> :: <dotted path> => <token exactly as written on the page>
#
# The token carries its product name on purpose. Binding the bare number would make the staleness
# direction a tautology — "4" appears in any page of prose — so the check would pass over a page
# that no longer mentions Behat at all. The version is the token's last whitespace-separated word.
#
# The gate (make php.lint.project-context) checks both directions:
#   - the manifest still starts with the token's version, so a bump that skips the page fails;
#   - the token still appears verbatim on the page, so rewording a cell without touching this file
#     fails rather than leaving a line guarding a claim nobody makes any more.
#
# What a green does NOT prove:
#   - Nothing about the third column of those tables. It is prose, it is where every measured drift
#     landed, and no cheap check can falsify it — reading the code is the only control.
#   - Nothing about a version the page states that has NO line here. The gate cannot derive the
#     universe: a manifest holds hundreds of entries and the page names a dozen, so completeness is
#     a review obligation, not a mechanical one. Adding a version to the page means adding it here.
#   - Nothing about anything pinned by digest rather than by manifest — Node and the base images.
#     The page names no digest value, so there is nothing to compare.
#   - A dotted path cannot address a manifest key that itself contains a dot. None does today.

